---
// Bare-domain (`/`) route. cire is multi-tenant, so there is no single "the"
// wedding to show at this address — every guest arrives on a per-wedding path
// (`/<slug>`, server-rendered by `[slug].astro`) from their own invite link.
// The bare domain therefore belongs to the marketing site, not to any one
// couple.
//
// This previously resolved the MOST-RECENTLY-CREATED wedding via
// `GET /api/primary-wedding` and redirected to it, which served one arbitrary
// couple's invite to every bare-domain visitor — and leaked whose invite was
// newest. That endpoint is gone; nothing here touches the API now, so the route
// has no failure mode and no neutral/error state to render.
//
// Any query string is deliberately NOT carried across: the only one that ever
// rode the bare domain was a `?code=` host-preview deep link, which is
// meaningless to the marketing site and shouldn't be forwarded off-origin.
//
// 302, not 301: where the bare domain points is a product decision we may
// revisit, and a permanent redirect would sit in browser caches indefinitely.
import { MARKETING_URL } from '../lib/invite'

return Astro.redirect(MARKETING_URL, 302)
---
